Subject: [PATCH 22/67] Strings.Pos with a negative start searches from 0

It indexed s[pos] with pos as given, an index trap (or a read before s
without -x) for a negative pos. Insert and Delete already count a
negative position as 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/Strings.Mod | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/runtime/Strings.Mod b/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
index 8eb7dc2f..55ff2b53 100644
--- a/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
+++ b/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@
 BEGIN
   n1 := Length(s); n2 := Length(pattern);
   IF n2 = 0 THEN RETURN 0 END ;
+  IF pos < 0 THEN pos := 0 END ;
   i := pos;
   WHILE i <= n1 - n2 DO
     IF s[i] = pattern[0] THEN
